time=2026-10-26T23:08:05.529Z level=INFO msg="model prompt" record=prov-2026-f86ede24 attempt=1 prompt="## The change\n\nthe regenerationOnly function reports whether a change is a pure re-render of sedum regions in governed files, with no change to record state.\n\n## Constraints on it\n\n- The function receives, in order: a pointer to a repo, the base revision string, the tree path string, a slice of all changed path strings and a pointer to the tagged record.Record\n- The function returns a boolean\n- The tagged record parameter is not used.\n- The function returns false when any changed path is a record file (recordFileID, check_run.go; parameters: a pointer to a repo and a path string; returns a string, non-empty for a record file)\n- The function returns false when stateExempt (check_run.go; parameters: a pointer to a repo and a path string; returns a boolean) is true for any changed path\n- Changed paths for which scope.Excluded (parameters: a path string and the repo's Config.ExcludePaths slice; returns a boolean) is true are ignored by the remaining steps\n- The function returns false when no governed path remains\n- For each governed path the function returns false when headHas (check_run.go; parameters: a pointer to a repo, a revision string and a path string; returns a boolean) says it is absent from the base\n- The staged file of a governed path is the tree path joined with the changed path converted to the operating system's separator\n- The function returns false when the staged file does not exist or cannot be read\n- The git command runs with the repo's Root as working directory\n- The git command's environment is the result of the repo's gitEnv method\n- The base content is the raw output bytes, untrimmed\n- The function returns false when the base content cannot be read\n- The function returns false when regionsAgree (parameters: base content string and staged content string; returns a boolean) is false for any governed path\n- The records to verify are the distinct record ids named by the regions of the staged content of the governed paths, in order of first appearance\n- The function returns false unless sedumCurrent (parameters: a pointer to a repo, the tree string and a record id string; returns a boolean) is true for each of those ids\n- The function returns true when all steps pass\n- The repo parameter is a pointer to the repo struct defined in common_run.go of package main\n- The repo's Root field is a string holding the absolute repository root path\n- The repo's Config.ExcludePaths field is a slice of strings\n- The repo's gitEnv method takes no arguments and returns the environment for git commands as a slice of strings\n- The base content is read by running git cat-file blob with the base, a colon, ./ and the path.\n- The ./ before the path makes git resolve the path relative to the repo root, which is the git command's working directory, rather than the git top level.\n- The function owns the imports of github.com/livecodelife/provenance/record and github.com/livecodelife/provenance/scope, each as a value import of a package of this module\n- The function uses os, os/exec and path/filepath, whose imports are owned by another record in the same file\n- The function takes the Record field of each marker returned by splitRegions (parameter: a string; returns the outside text string, a slice of regionMarker and a boolean)\n\n## Supplementary context\n\nThis section is supplied by the caller, not by the record. It is advisory: it does not add to or change what the record authorized, and the files below remain the only ones the actions may reach.\n\nSelections made for this change on an earlier run (context only; they are not applied):\n\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/regen_run.go\",\"path\":\"github.com/livecodelife/provenance/record\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/regen_run.go\",\"path\":\"github.com/livecodelife/provenance/scope\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"setFunction\",\"kwargs\":{\"code\":\"func regenerationOnly(r *repo, base string, treePath string, changed []string, _ *record.Record) bool {\\n\\tvar governed []string\\n\\tfor _, p := range changed {\\n\\t\\tif recordFileID(r, p) != \\\"\\\" {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn false\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tif stateExempt(r, p) {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn false\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tif scope.Excluded(p, r.Config.ExcludePaths) {\\n\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tgoverned = append(governed, p)\\n\\t}\\n\\tif len(governed) == 0 {\\n\\t\\treturn false\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tvar stagedAll []string\\n\\tfor _, p := range governed {\\n\\t\\tif !headHas(r, base, p) {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn false\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tstaged := filepath.Join(treePath, filepath.FromSlash(p))\\n\\t\\tdata, err := os.ReadFile(staged)\\n\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn false\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tcmd := exec.Command(\\\"git\\\", \\\"cat-file\\\", \\\"blob\\\", base+\\\":./\\\"+p)\\n\\t\\tcmd.Dir = r.Root\\n\\t\\tcmd.Env = r.gitEnv()\\n\\t\\tbaseOut, err := cmd.Output()\\n\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn false\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tif !regionsAgree(string(baseOut), string(data)) {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn false\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tstagedAll = append(stagedAll, string(data))\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tseen := map[string]bool{}\\n\\tvar ids []string\\n\\tfor _, content := range stagedAll {\\n\\t\\t_, markers, _ := splitRegions(content)\\n\\t\\tfor _, m := range markers {\\n\\t\\t\\tif !seen[m.Record] {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tseen[m.Record] = true\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tids = append(ids, m.Record)\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\tfor _, id := range ids {\\n\\t\\tif !sedumCurrent(r, treePath, id) {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn false\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\treturn true\\n}\",\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/regen_run.go\",\"name\":\"regenerationOnly\"}}\n\n## Already present\n\nThese regions already exist in the files below and belong to other changes. Do not select them: an action that resolves to one of them would conflict with the change that owns it.\n\n- cmd/provenance/regen_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/regen_run.go\",\"path\":\"os\"} (owned by prov-2026-351c5684; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/regen_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/regen_run.go\",\"path\":\"os/exec\"} (owned by prov-2026-351c5684; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/regen_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/regen_run.go\",\"path\":\"path/filepath\"} (owned by prov-2026-351c5684; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/regen_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/regen_run.go\",\"path\":\"strings\"} (owned by prov-2026-351c5684; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/regen_run.go: setFunction {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/regen_run.go\",\"name\":\"splitRegions\"} (owned by prov-2026-0b95d9fb; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/regen_run.go: setFunction {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/regen_run.go\",\"name\":\"regionsAgree\"} (owned by prov-2026-342fc2b3; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/regen_run.go: setFunction {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/regen_run.go\",\"name\":\"sedumCurrent\"} (owned by prov-2026-351c5684; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/regen_run.go: setType {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/regen_run.go\",\"name\":\"regionMarker\"} (owned by prov-2026-fd7c2130; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/regen_run.go: setFunction {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/regen_run.go\",\"name\":\"sedumMissing\"} (owned by prov-2026-b171a7da; do not select)\n\n## Files\n\nThese files exist and are the only ones the actions below may reach:\n\n- cmd/provenance/regen_run.go (package go; injection points: decls, imports)\n\n## Actions\n\n{\n  \"actions\": [\n    {\n      \"action\": \"addImport\",\n      \"package\": \"go\",\n      \"description\": \"Imports one package.\",\n      \"kwargs\": {\n        \"file\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The Go file to write into. It must be one of the authorized files.\"\n        },\n        \"path\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The import path.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"anchor\": [\n        \"imports\"\n      ],\n      \"requires\": [\n        \"path\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"action\": \"setConst\",\n      \"package\": \"go\",\n      \"description\": \"Defines one package-level constant, replacing an earlier version of it.\",\n      \"kwargs\": {\n        \"code\": {\n          \"type\": \"literal\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The whole const declaration, as gofmt-formatted Go.\"\n        },\n        \"file\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The Go file to write into. It must be one of the authorized files.\"\n        },\n        \"name\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The constant's name.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"anchor\": [\n        \"decls\"\n      ],\n      \"requires\": [\n        \"code\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"action\": \"setFunction\",\n      \"package\": \"go\",\n      \"description\": \"Defines one top-level function, replacing an earlier version of it.\",\n      \"kwargs\": {\n        \"code\": {\n          \"type\": \"literal\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The whole function declaration, signature and body, as gofmt-formatted Go.\"\n        },\n        \"file\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The Go file to write into. It must be one of the authorized files.\"\n        },\n        \"name\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The function's name.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"anchor\": [\n        \"decls\"\n      ],\n      \"requires\": [\n        \"code\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"action\": \"setMethod\",\n      \"package\": \"go\",\n      \"description\": \"Defines one method, replacing an earlier version of it.\",\n      \"kwargs\": {\n        \"code\": {\n          \"type\": \"literal\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The whole method declaration, receiver, signature and body, as gofmt-formatted Go.\"\n        },\n        \"file\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The Go file to write into. It must be one of the authorized files.\"\n        },\n        \"name\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The method's name.\"\n        },\n        \"receiver\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The receiver's type name, without a pointer star.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"anchor\": [\n        \"decls\"\n      ],\n      \"requires\": [\n        \"code\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"action\": \"setType\",\n      \"package\": \"go\",\n      \"description\": \"Defines one named type, replacing an earlier version of it.\",\n      \"kwargs\": {\n        \"code\": {\n          \"type\": \"literal\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The whole type declaration, as gofmt-formatted Go.\"\n        },\n        \"file\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The Go file to write into. It must be one of the authorized files.\"\n        },\n        \"name\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The type's name.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"anchor\": [\n        \"decls\"\n      ],\n      \"requires\": [\n        \"code\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"action\": \"setVar\",\n      \"package\": \"go\",\n      \"description\": \"Defines one package-level variable, replacing an earlier version of it.\",\n      \"kwargs\": {\n        \"code\": {\n          \"type\": \"literal\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The whole var declaration, as gofmt-formatted Go.\"\n        },\n        \"file\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The Go file to write into. It must be one of the authorized files.\"\n        },\n        \"name\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The variable's name.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"anchor\": [\n        \"decls\"\n      ],\n      \"requires\": [\n        \"code\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n"
